            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/README.md",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Are the associations documented in Inventory.Item \"generic\" in the sense they could apply to other inventory interfaces? For eg it has the controlled_by association which required xyz.openbmc_project.Control.Valve. Should this association be documented in Inventory.Item and in Inventory.Valve, or does one of them suffice?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/README.md",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If something is documented in Item it does not need to be documented in sub-items.\n\nI do not know why we ended up with Control.Valve referencing Item.Valve but Item referencing Control.Valve.  This should be fixed by @paligill@gmail.com (outside the scope of this change)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/README.md",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I see the reverse associations are documented under Item.interface.yaml if the forward association endpoint name is common across multiple sub inventory item types, probably to avoid duplication?\nThe other option could be to move it into Item/Valve.interface.yaml"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/README.md",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, if it can be used by multiple sub-item types I usually suggest it goes under Item.  I'm fine either way you want to do it, as long as it is consistent.  I don't remember how we ended up with it Item itself but maybe you could revive that discussion and see if there was any good reason for it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/README.md",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
